<title>GERMANY: Official German grain intervention offers detailed.</title>
<headline>Official German grain intervention offers detailed.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain offers in the 1996/97 (Nov/May) intervention season totalled 1.58 million tonnes on June 16, versus 1.68 million a year earlier, intervention board BLE said.</p>
<p>A BLE source said the deadline for offers had expired on Saturday, May 31, but some were still being processed and sellers were also able to withdraw offers.</p>
<p>BLE gave the following breakdown of offers in tonnes --</p>
<p>			    June 16, 1997   May 30, 1997 June 16,1996</p>
<p>    soft wheat	    247,364	  142,404	 11,750</p>
<p>    rye		     769,293	  711,686	938,189</p>
<p>    barley		  550,829	  447,805	731,859</p>
<p>    maize		     7,900	    2,540	---</p>
<p>    TOTAL		 1,575,386	1,304,435    1,681,798</p>
<p>BLE also detailed actual stocks as of June 13 at 1,681,783 tonnes.</p>
<p>This included volumes left over from previous seasons.</p>
<p>On June 14, 1996, stocks totalled 2,865,570 tonnes.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
